counterfactuals.output:
A computer-implemented method comprising:

receiving, by a network device and over a communication network, motion data generated by an audio/video recording and communication device, the motion data representing detected movement within a field of view of the audio/video recording and communication device;

determining, by the network device, a location associated with the detected movement based at least in part on the received motion data;

comparing, by the network device, the determined location with an intrusion-zone definition identifying a designated portion of the field of view;

determining that an intrusion-zone condition is satisfied when the detected movement is located within the designated portion and satisfies one or more intrusion criteria; and

responsive to determining that the intrusion-zone condition is satisfied, transmitting, by the network device, a control signal that causes a security system to perform a security action.

The security action may comprise entering an alarm state, activating an audible or visual annunciator, initiating or preserving an audio/video recording, locking an access-control device, illuminating a premises area, transmitting a notification, or requesting verification by a user or monitoring service. The intrusion criteria may include one or more of an object classification, a duration of movement, a direction of travel, a time-based rule, an occupancy state, or an armed status of the security system.
